# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000977> (pleura)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0-683-40008-8") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "MP:0010820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "UBERON:cjm") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Pulmonary_pleurae") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1231") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000977> "The invaginated serous membrane that surrounds the lungs (the visceral portion) and lines the walls of the pleural cavity (parietal portion).")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000007> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000977> "pleural")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000977> "In MA, is_a cavity lining (which we equate to parietal). In FMA, is_a (viscous) serous membrane (which includes mesothelium plus connective tissue). Note the MA structure should probably be associated with the mesothelium of pleura in FMA. JB/EHDAA2 argues the term 'pleura' is best used for the mesothelial lining (thus excluding connective tissue). See https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/86")
